    "description": "The Opportunity The EiE Officer will play a critical role in supporting and facilitating the effective implementation of the ECHO project in emergency and crisis-affected contexts. The officer will focus on integrating education, protection, and WASH approaches into teaching and learning, promoting children's access to quality education opportunities in these settings. The role involves coordination, capacity building, monitoring, and reporting to achieve the project's goals. The post holder will work closely with school management and government stakeholders, including Regional Education Bureaus, Woreda Education Offices, NGOs, and INGOs within the project areas. The position has a direct reporting line to the Emergency Project Coordinator. Key Accountabilities Include; Assessment (15%) Design and implement rapid needs assessments in emergency contexts to identify gaps in education implementation. Use assessment findings to inform the design and adaptation of project activities, ensuring they are responsive to the needs of children and communities. Collaborate with external evaluators and researchers to conduct in-depth studies on the effectiveness/Impact of education methodologies in emergency settings. Develop and administer tools for assessing the quality of education environments and the capacity of teachers. Analyse assessment data to identify trends, challenges, and opportunities for improving project outcomes. Share assessment results with stakeholders, including government agencies, donors, and community members, to promote evidence-based decision-making. Project Implementation (40%) Lead and follow up the implementation of education in emergency activities under the ECHO-funded project, ensuring alignment with the project’s goals and objectives. Integrate methodologies into education in emergency programs to enhance children’s learning outcomes and psychosocial well-being. Support the development and distribution of learning materials and resources for children, teachers, and caregivers. Organize and facilitate training sessions for teachers, PTSA/CMC, and community members. Build the capacity of teachers, school administrators, and PTSA/CMC/ to deliver quality education in emergency contexts. Provide ongoing coaching and mentoring to teachers and PTSA/CMC to ensure the effective implementation of emergency education methodologies. Collaborate with local education authorities to strengthen formal and non-formal education systems and policies. Monitoring, Reporting & Evaluation (30%) Together with the EPC, implement the developed monitoring and evaluation (M&E) frameworks to track the progress and impact of project activities. Conduct regular field visits to monitor project implementation, ensuring activities are on track and aligned with project objectives. Collect, analyse, and interpret data on project indicators to assess the effectiveness of interventions and identify areas for improvement. Collect and prepare high-quality reports, including progress reports, donor reports, and case studies, to document project achievements and challenges. Use M&E findings to inform decision-making, improve project strategies, and ensure accountability to stakeholders. Support the documentation of best practices, lessons learned, and success stories to contribute to organizational learning and knowledge sharing. Support other staff and volunteers in monitoring program progress against indicators in grants Information and Coordination (15%) Act as the primary liaison between Plan International Ethiopia and local government authorities, ensuring alignment with national and regional education policies and frameworks. Represent Plan International Ethiopia in education coordination meetings, clusters, and working groups at the regional and national levels. Foster partnerships with local NGOs, community-based organizations, and other stakeholders to enhance the reach and impact of the project. Collaborate with other Plan International projects and teams to ensure integration and synergy across programs, particularly in areas of child protection, gender equality, and disaster risk reduction. Engage with parents, caregivers, and community leaders to raise awareness about the importance of education and secure their support for project activities. Work closely with the consortium partners to ensure harmonized approaches and shared learning across project sites. Facilitate joint planning and review meetings with stakeholders to ensure transparency, accountability, and collective ownership of project outcomes. Advocate for the inclusion of education and home-based education in local and national education policies and strategies, leveraging evidence from the project.",
