    "datePosted": "2026-11-10T07:00:01.000Z",
    "description": "Consultancy Services for Translation of the “Empowering Selam” Comic Book Project: Joint Action to Promote Equality, Peace, and Healing in Ethiopia Implementing Organizations: EURIKA, N4ED, and IDS Consortium: Sew Mehon – Alliance of Ethiopian Local CSOs 1. Background The Sewmehon Alliance is implementing the project \"Joint Action to Promote Equality, Peace, and Healing in Ethiopia,\" funded by CSIF II. This project aims to strengthen gender equality, peacebuilding, and human rights through community-based, participatory, and culturally relevant approaches. The project is implemented across Tigray, Amhara, South Ethiopia, Benishangul-Gumuz, Harari, and Addis Ababa. As part of the project’s awareness-raising and community engagement activities, the consortium is developing a comic book titled “Empowering Selam.” The comic book aims to communicate key messages related to gender equality, human rights, peacebuilding, and the prevention of gender-based violence (GBV) in an engaging and accessible format, particularly for young people and community members. To ensure that the comic book is accessible to communities in the target regions, the consortium is seeking qualified translators to translate the finalized comic book from Amharic to English, Tigrigna,Gaammo, and Afaan Oromoo . 2. Objective of the Consultancy The main objective of the translator is to provide a high-quality, accurate, culturally appropriate, and reader-friendly translation of the “Empowering Selam” comic book into the assigned local language(s). The translation should preserve the meaning, tone, key messages, and context of the original Amharic version while ensuring that the language is natural and easily understood by the intended audience. 3. Scope of Work The selected translator(s) will be responsible for: Reviewing the finalized Amharic version of the comic book before translation. Translating all text within the comic book (including dialogue, captions, sound effects, and narrative text) into the assigned local language. Maintaining the intended meaning, tone, character voices, dialogue style, and key messages of the original content. Ensuring that terminology related to gender equality, human rights, peacebuilding, and GBV is accurate and culturally appropriate for the target audience. Adapting expressions, idioms, and dialogue where necessary to make the content natural and engaging for local readers. Ensuring consistency in character names, terminology, key concepts, and core messages throughout the comic book. Identifying any culturally sensitive or potentially unclear content and discussing necessary adjustments with the project team. Reviewing the translated version and making corrections based on feedback from the project team. Providing the final, clean, and editable translated version in the format requested by the consortium. 4. Expected Deliverable One complete and professionally translated version of the “Empowering Selam” comic book in the assigned local language, formatted cleanly with all dialogue, captions, and text properly aligned. Participation in a brief review or validation process with the project team to ensure translation quality and appropriateness. Interested candidates are invited to submit the following application documents: Updated CV , highlighting relevant translation and creative writing experience. Brief technical proposal , explaining their understanding of the assignment, proposed methodology, and target language capabilities. Samples of previous translation work , preferably involving creative, educational, advocacy, or community-based materials. Financial proposal , clearly specifying the unit rate per word (ETB / word) for each target language applied for (e.g., rate per word for Tigrigna, Afaan Oromoo, Gaammo, or English). Contact details of at least two professional references. Evaluation Criteria Applications will be evaluated based on: Criteria Weight Relevant academic qualifications 10% Professional translation experience 20% Experience translating creative/educational materials 20% Knowledge of gender, human rights, peacebuilding and related themes 15% Quality of submitted translation sample 15% Financial proposal ( per-word rate ) 20% Total 100%",
